council — third-party asset attribution
========================================

3D model
--------
The rotating 3D head used by the application's themed display mode is derived
from the model "Evangelion Unit 01 head Printable" by ngkirto
  https://sketchfab.com/3d-models/evangelion-unit-01-head-printable-3a8d3a39f72740fcb08760a12f97b0a3
licensed under CC-BY-4.0
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Changes: the mesh was decimated into a compact point cloud
(internal/tui/anim/mesh_data.go). The original mesh is not redistributed.

Model pricing
-------------
internal/pricing is a behaviour-preserving Go port of the model-price lookup in
codeburn by AgentSeal
  https://github.com/getagentseal/codeburn
licensed under the MIT License (Copyright (c) 2026 AgentSeal).

Ported/adapted logic: canonical-name and explicit alias lookup, per-token
clamping, and LiteLLM cache/snapshot handling (internal/pricing/pricing.go).
Council intentionally omits Codeburn's fuzzy/newest-family matching for run
ledger pricing. Copied data: the bundled LiteLLM price snapshot and gap-fill
table (internal/pricing/data/{litellm-snapshot,pricing-fallback}.json),
themselves derived from BerriAI/litellm, and the model-alias table
(internal/pricing/aliases.go).
